<title>USA: TABLE - Xerox Corp Q2 net income up 15 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Xerox Corp Q2 net income up 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Call Q2 consensus estimate $0.89.</p>
<p>			   3 Mos ended 6/30 %    6 Mos ended 6/30 %</p>
<p>			  1997    1996  Growth     1997  1996 Growth</p>
<p> Revenues	   $ 4,356 $ 4,217  3%	$ 8,378 $ 8,145  3%</p>
<p>NET INCOME(LOSS)</p>
<p>  Continuing Opers    337     293  15	    607    530  15</p>
<p>  Disc Operations     337     293  15	    607    530  15</p>
<p>PRIMARY EPS</p>
<p>    Continuing Ops   1.00    0.85  18	   1.78   1.53  16</p>
<p>    Discontinued Ops   --	--		   --     --</p>
<p> Primary EPS	   1.00    0.85  18	   1.78   1.53  16</p>
<p>FULLY DILUTED EPS</p>
<p>  Continuing Ops     0.94    0.81  16	   1.69   1.46  16</p>
<p>  Discontinued Ops     --	--		   --     --</p>
<p> Fully Diluted EPS   0.94    0.81  16	   1.69   1.46  16</p>
<p>		  (in millions, except per-share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1997 Q2 EPS of $0.94 includes $0.04 a share from acquisition of Rank Group's remaining interest in Rank Xerox.</p>
<p>Q2 income increased 15 percent to $337 million, including $13 million as a result of the Rank Xerox transaction.</p>
